cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  paper it accompanies (see `preferred-citation`).
title: >-
  Trajectory analysis code for long-term NIR single-particle tracking with
  Au42 gold quantum needles
abstract: >-
  Analysis code accompanying the study of long-term near-infrared
  single-particle tracking with atomically precise gold quantum needles
  Au42(PET)32. Contains three pipelines: (i) reconstruction of trajectories
  from per-frame particle positions, including separation of instrument
  vibration from sample-derived collective motion before linking;
  (ii) DC-MSS (divide-and-conquer moment scaling spectrum) segmentation and
  motion classification, with the Monte-Carlo threshold calibration used for
  classification; and (iii) directional-correlation analysis of velocity and
  direction autocorrelation as an independent check on the DC-MSS classes.
type: software
